# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces a CRLF
# working tree (~439 of 466 tracked files), which broke several tests that read
# repo files through `include_str!` and one exported frontend utility. Those
# were fixed in code where the contract is genuinely "handle either ending";
# this pins the repo's own files so the question stops arising.
#
# `text=auto` lets git DETECT text vs binary, so the 27 files it already treats
# as binary are untouched. `eol=lf` checks text out as LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
